  <prompt>
    Implement FR-24: a deterministic `DocxAnnotationWriter` service that renders pending Compose
    annotations (accepted track-change insertions/deletions + user/AI comments) into a `.docx` as
    native Open XML `&lt;w:comment&gt;` + `&lt;w:ins&gt;` / `&lt;w:del&gt;` elements, then a `POST
    /api/compose/document/{spe-id}/push-annotations` endpoint that persists the rewritten file to SPE
    via `SpeFileStore.ReplaceFileContentAsUserAsync` with an `If-Match` etag. This is a purely
    deterministic operation (NO LLM call) — the value is Word for Web rendering pushed annotations
    natively. The hard part is the edge cases (comments-before-track-changes ordering; paragraph-
    boundary `&lt;w:del&gt;`; monotonic revision-id/author/date metadata) captured by Spike 5 and adeu's
    bug-numbered wisdom (design §6.2). Spike 5 (dep 005) validated the Open XML write → SPE → Word
    for Web render path; this task productionizes it.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 developer fluent in the Microsoft Open XML SDK 3.x (`DocumentFormat.OpenXml`) and
    OOXML WordprocessingML revision/comment markup, plus Minimal API endpoint authoring and the
    Spaarke SPE facade (`SpeFileStore` / `ISpeFileOperations`). Comfortable encoding hard-won
    edge-case handling as `// EDGE-N:` numbered comments.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A `DocxAnnotationWriter` in `Services/Compose/` that, given a source `.docx` byte stream + a
    structured set of Compose annotations, produces a byte-identical-where-untouched `.docx`
    carrying valid `&lt;w:comment&gt;` and `&lt;w:ins&gt;`/`&lt;w:del&gt;` markup that Word for Web renders natively
    with correct author/date/id; plus an authorized `POST
    /api/compose/document/{spe-id}/push-annotations` endpoint that saves the result to SPE with
    optimistic-concurrency (`If-Match`). Matching unit tests in
    `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/` cover the ordering, paragraph-boundary, and
    metadata-uniqueness edge cases plus malformed-input and etag-conflict negatives.
  </goal>

