  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">NO `Microsoft.Graph` types above the `SpeFileStore`/Infrastructure facade. `DocxAnnotationWriter` operates on byte streams; all SPE read/write goes through `SpeFileStore.ReplaceFileContentAsUserAsync` / the download facade — never a `GraphServiceClient`, `DriveItem`, or other `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">The push-annotations endpoint uses `.RequireAuthorization()` (inherited from the `/api/compose` group) and resource authorization via endpoint filter where applicable — no global middleware for the resource check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriter` MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`, executor types, or `IConsumerRoutingService`. This is a deterministic DOCX operation with zero AI reach. Tier-1 NetArchTest enforces.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Keep DI additions minimal. `DocxAnnotationWriter` may be a single registered service; internal helpers (revision-id generator, ordering pass) need not be DI-registered.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029 / CLAUDE.md §10">Measure BFF publish size after adding the Open XML SDK: `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report absolute compressed size + delta vs 49.63 MB baseline. ≥+5 MB single-task delta → justify; ≥55 MB cumulative → flag architecture review. Verify no new HIGH CVE (`dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`). State the PDB convention when reporting.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07">Only MIT runtime deps — Open XML SDK 3.x + Codeuctivity.OpenXmlPowerTools. Zero commercial license fees.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">Every new/modified `Services/Compose/` service ships matching unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / §10 Placement Justification">State the Placement Justification for the new service + endpoint in the PR description, citing bff-extensions.md decision criteria.</constraint>
  </constraints>

