    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj (Open XML SDK + OpenXmlPowerTools packages)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriterTests.cs</output>
    <output type="report">Publish-size absolute + delta; CVE scan result; Placement Justification</output>
  </outputs>

  <justification>
    <existing>No existing service writes OOXML comment/revision markup — `ComposeService` handles SPE load/save/promote only; `DocxAnnotationReader` (task 051) is the read direction. No overlap.</existing>
    <extension>Cannot be folded into `ComposeService`: that class is the SPE-lifecycle facade with a distinct responsibility; annotation authoring is a cohesive, testable OOXML concern with heavy edge-case surface that warrants its own unit-tested unit (SRP). The endpoint reuses `ComposeEndpoints.cs` and `SpeFileStore` — no new SPE plumbing.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, every accepted AI suggestion and comment stays locked inside Compose — Word for Web shows none of it natively, defeating the competitive-parity requirement (design §2.4). Concrete failing contract: FR-24 acceptance "Word for Web renders pushed comments + track changes natively" cannot be met.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Given a source `.docx` + a comment + an insertion/deletion pair, the writer emits valid `&lt;w:comment&gt;`, `&lt;w:ins&gt;`, `&lt;w:del&gt;` with correct author/date and a monotonic per-document revision id, and Word for Web renders them natively (validated against the Spike 5 recipe).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Comments are emitted before track changes in the pipeline order; a unit test asserts the ordering rule.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A paragraph-boundary deletion deletes the paragraph mark via `w:pPr/w:rPr/w:del`; a unit test asserts the EDGE handler fires.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`POST /api/compose/document/{spe-id}/push-annotations` requires authorization and persists via `ReplaceFileContentAsUserAsync` with the caller's `If-Match` etag, returning the new version.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a malformed/non-DOCX input returns 400 ProblemDetails, not an unhandled exception.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a stale `If-Match` etag (SPE version changed under the caller) returns 412 and does NOT partially write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriter` injects no AI-internal type (NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` type appears in `Services/Compose/` (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported absolute + delta vs 49.63 MB baseline, ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; only MIT deps added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Matching unit tests exist and pass; BFF build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Completed 2026-07-09 (FULL rigor, opus @ xhigh). BFF build green (0 errors); 13 new DocxAnnotationWriter
    tests pass (incl. OpenXmlValidator Office2019 = 0 errors, closing Spike 5 static-validity criterion);
    99 Services.Compose unit tests green (no regression); Tier-1 ADR013_ComposeFacadeTests + ADR-007
    Endpoints-vs-Graph arch tests PASS.

    FILES:
    - NEW src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriter.cs — pure byte[]→byte[] OOXML
      annotation writer (w:ins/w:del/w:comment). Reuses TrackChangeKind; DocxAnnotation contract mirrors
      target_text/new_text. EDGE-1 comments-before-track-changes; EDGE-2 paragraph-mark deletion via
      w:pPr/w:rPr/w:del; EDGE-3 monotonic id seeded past existing; EDGE-4 DeletedText not Text. Thread-safe
      singleton (per-call AnnotationSession). DocxAnnotationException{MalformedDocument→400, TargetNotFound→422}.
    - NEW src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeConcurrencyExceptions.cs — EtagPreconditionFailedException(412),
      DocumentLockedByWordException(423). Facade translation of Graph errors (ADR-007; no Graph type leaks).
    - MOD Infrastructure/Graph/{ISpeFileOperations,SpeFileStore,UploadSessionManager}.cs — added If-Match OVERLOAD
      of ReplaceFileContentAsUserAsync (Spike 7 G-1/G-2: closes the C-2 gap — as-built method had NO If-Match).
      Additive overload; existing 5-arg callers/mocks untouched. 423/412 caught → typed exceptions.
    - MOD Services/Compose/{IComposeService,ComposeService}.cs — PushAnnotationsAsync orchestration (download→
      annotate→If-Match write), mirrors SaveAsync. ComposeService gains DocxAnnotationWriter dep.
    - MOD Infrastructure/DI/ComposeModule.cs — AddSingleton<DocxAnnotationWriter> (unconditional; consumer +
      endpoint also unconditional → no §F.1 asymmetric-registration risk).
    - MOD Api/ComposeEndpoints.cs — POST /api/compose/document/{documentSpeId}/push-annotations (route #9),
      handler maps DocxAnnotationException→400/422, 412, 423, 404/403/500. (Exception types fully-qualified
      inline to avoid churning the using-block during a concurrent FR-03 edit of the same file.)
    - NEW tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationWriterTests.cs — 13 domain-logic tests
      (ADR-038 KEEP; no transport mocks; real docx round-trip + validator).

    DEVIATION (directional mode, Spike 5-grounded): POML Step 1 said add DocumentFormat.OpenXml + Codeuctivity.
    OpenXmlPowerTools. Spike 5 VALIDATED OpenXml 3.4.1 is ALREADY referenced and OpenXmlPowerTools is NOT needed
    for the writer path → ZERO packages added, ~0 publish-size delta. Publish (Release) = 45.18 MB compressed
    incl PDBs (≤60 ceiling; baseline 49.63). No new HIGH CVE (Kiota.Abstractions HIGH is pre-existing transitive,
    not introduced here). PLACEMENT: writer is a new deterministic OOXML unit in Services/Compose (cannot fold
    into ComposeService per SRP); endpoint reuses ComposeEndpoints + SpeFileStore — no new SPE plumbing. NO AI
    reach (ADR-013 arch test green). Runtime Word-for-Web native render remains the Spike 5 §5 / Spike 7 §7
    integration recipe (real SPE container) — out of headless unit scope.
  </notes>

